@startuml
title Runtime network services around the packet streamer

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "TTC layer" as caller

component "networkSession\n(facade)" as session
component "dataService\n(TTC byte stream)" as data
component "breakResetService\n(marker watcher)" as reset
component "notificationService\n(short-poll consumer)" as notification

queue "DATA handoff\n(capacity 1)" as dataQueue
queue "MARKER handoff\n(capacity 1 + acknowledgment)" as markerQueue
queue "CONTROL buffer" as controlQueue

caller --> session : session API
session --> data : read / write / flush
session --> reset : CancelOperation
session --> notification : CheckInbandNotification

component "packetStreamer\n(single transport reader;\nserialized packet writer)" as streamer

streamer -left-> dataQueue : NSPTDA
dataQueue -left-> data : readDataPacket()
data --> streamer : writePacket(DATA)

streamer -left-> markerQueue : NSPTMK; wait for acknowledgment
markerQueue -left-> reset : watchMarkers()
reset --> streamer : acknowledge marker
reset ..> streamer : pause / resume DATA delivery
reset --> streamer : writePacket(MARKER)

streamer -left-> controlQueue : NSPTCNL
controlQueue -left-> notification : readControlPacket()\n(50 microsecond poll)

' Keep services, handoffs, and the streamer in left-to-right columns.
session -[hidden]right-> dataQueue
data -[hidden]right-> dataQueue
reset -[hidden]right-> markerQueue
notification -[hidden]right-> controlQueue

component "networkTransport\n(packet decode / encode,\ncompression, adapter I/O)" as transport
component "TCP / TCPS adapter" as adapter
cloud "Oracle Net server" as server

streamer --> transport : sole reader callback\nserialized writer callback
transport --> adapter : Receive / Send
adapter <--> server : Oracle Net packets

note bottom of streamer
  DATA and MARKER use bounded handoffs, applying backpressure.
  CONTROL packets are buffered separately until polled.
  A marker acknowledgment lets the reader continue after break-reset handles it.
end note

note top of session
  Created after ACCEPT. Connection negotiation uses a separate,
  synchronous negotiationStreamer before runtime services start.
end note

note bottom of session
  Disconnect closes the packet streamer, joins the marker watcher,
  then disconnects the adapter.
end note

@enduml
